  "updated": "2026-10-13",
  "summary": "Sources for Moluntha’s role, the Treaty of Fort Finney, Logan’s October 1786 raid and McGary’s killing of Moluntha, with each side’s motives. Town counts and dates differ between sources.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Shawnee side",
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Mekoche ceremonial leader from 1780; Americans mistook the role for ‘king’.",
          "sources": [
            "wp-mol"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Signed Fort Finney reluctantly, Jan. 1786; most Shawnees rejected it; message to British: ‘We have been cheated by the Americans.’",
          "sources": [
            "wp-mol",
            "wp-finney"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Flew a US flag and held the treaty when he surrendered.",
          "sources": [
            "wp-mol",
            "wp-raid"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Kentucky side",
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "After raids and counter-raids along the Ohio, Kentucky militia launched a two-pronged 1786 campaign under Clark and Logan.",
          "sources": [
            "wp-nwiw"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Logan led about 700 militia; McGary, bitter over Blue Licks, killed Moluntha; court-martialed and suspended one year.",
          "sources": [
            "wp-mcgary",
            "wp-mol"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ensign Ebenezer Denny: ‘none but old men, women and children… the men were literally murdered.’",
          "sources": [
            "wp-raid"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Contested details",
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Seven towns and Oct. 6 (Moluntha, McGary articles) vs. thirteen villages and Oct. 12 (Logan’s raid infobox).",
          "sources": [
            "wp-mol",
            "wp-raid",
            "wp-mcgary"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Unpinned: the towns were in present Ohio, and the story centers on Moluntha, not the Limestone launch point.",
          "sources": []
        }
      ]
    }
